Spec: TenantInstance

Purpose:
  Carry the full cluster-side contract of one tenant-package installation: declare the install
    coordinate (`jukebox`, `category`, `package`, opaque `options`, optional `initFrom` restore
    source), track per-stage install progress across the richest @ConditionsType set of the CRD
    family — including the tenant-flow `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup` stages — in
    @TenantInstanceStatus through @ApplicationCondition records, resolve the tenant identity
    (name, namespaces, published service names) shared by scripts and flow code, and register
    @TenantInstance with its full accessor and mutator bridge onto package @rhai::Engine
    instances via @tenant_rhai_register.

Owns:
  ./instancetenant.rs

References:
  ./instance_macros.sdd — owns the semantics of every condition constructor, status setter,
    merge-patch, event, gate and Rhai bridge the macros attach to this type; this spec names the
    attached surface by name only.

Must:
  The @kube::CustomResource derive over @TenantInstanceSpec generates the @TenantInstance
    resource kind `TenantInstance` in group `vynil.solidite.fr`, version `v1`, namespaced
    scope, shortname `vti`, plural `tenantinstances`, with status type @TenantInstanceStatus and
    CRD doc `Custom resource representing an Vynil tenant package installation`.
  The CRD printer columns are, in order and by `jsonPath`: `Juke` -> `.spec.jukebox`,
    `cat` -> `.spec.category`, `pkg` -> `.spec.package`, `tag` -> `.status.tag`,
    `last_updated` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.type == 'Ready')].lastTransitionTime`
    (column type `date`, format `date-time`; the other six columns are type `string`),
    `stage` -> `.status.conditions[-1:].type`,
    `errors` -> `.status.conditions[?(@.status == 'False')].message`.
  Wire keys are fixed: the spec keys are `jukebox`, `category`, `package`, `initFrom` and
    `options`; @InitFrom keys are `secretName`, `subPath`, `snapshot` and `version` with
    `snapshot` the only key required at deserialization; the status keys are `conditions`,
    `tag`, `digest`, `tfstate`, `rhaistate`, `befores`, `vitals`, `scalables`, `others`, `posts`
    and `services`; @ApplicationCondition serializes camelCase keys `lastTransitionTime`,
    `message`, `type` (fixed by the @serde rename on @ApplicationCondition::condition_type),
    `status` and `generation`; @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus serialize as bare variant
    strings with @Default selecting `Ready` and `True`. Nothing in this file interprets
    `initFrom` or `options` contents.
  The module expands @impl_condition_common! and @impl_condition_children! at module scope plus
    @impl_instance_common!(TenantInstance, "TenantInstance") and @impl_instance_befores!
    (TenantInstance); @impl_condition_crds! and @impl_instance_crds! are deliberately not
    expanded, so this type carries no CRD-stage surface, its @ConditionsType omits `CrdApplied`,
    and @tenant_rhai_register registers no crd functions.
  Every @ConditionsType variant named by the two expanded condition macros exists in this
    module's enum — `Ready`, `Installed`, `AgentStarted`, `TofuInstalled`, `RhaiApplied`,
    `BeforeApplied`, `VitalApplied`, `ScalableApplied`, `OtherApplied`, `PostApplied`,
    `InitFrom`, `ScheduleBackup` — satisfying the macro declaration contract; the children and
    `InitFrom`/`ScheduleBackup` stages are carried only by this CRD and its `ServiceInstance`
    sibling, never by `SystemInstance`. The two remaining variants `Backuped` and `Restored`
    are declared (and visible in the generated schema) but named by no constructor or setter
    here (see Tasks).
  Every mutator attached by @impl_instance_common! patches the `status` subresource as a
    @kube::api::Patch::Merge carrying `apiVersion` `vynil.solidite.fr/v1` and the kind string
    `TenantInstance` — the @impl_instance_common! call-site literal — so the server replaces
    only the keys present in the patch; the keys ever written for this type are among
    `conditions`, `tag`, `digest`, `tfstate`, `rhaistate`, `services`, `befores`, `vitals`,
    `scalables`, `others` and `posts`, and `crds` is never written. Events published against
    the instance object ref follow the per-stage table in ./instance_macros.sdd.
  @TenantInstance::have_child answers `true` exactly when a status is present and at least one
    probe succeeds: `rhaistate` is `@Some` or `tfstate` is `@Some` regardless of content, or any
    of `befores`, `vitals`, `others`, `scalables`, `posts` is `@Some` and non-empty; a missing
    status answers `false`.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name reads the tenant identity from the instance namespace: with
    no `metadata.namespace` it fails with @crate::Error::Other carrying the exact text
    `TenantInstance has no namespace`; otherwise it fetches the @Namespace metadata
    cluster-wide and, when the namespace carries the label key from process environment
    `TENANT_LABEL` (read on every call, default `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant`), returns that label
    value, falling back to the instance namespace name when there are no labels or no such
    label.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces returns every namespace owned by the tenant: with the
    label present it lists namespace metadata with the equality selector
    `{label-key}=={tenant-value}` and collects the present names; without the label, or without
    labels at all, it returns exactly the instance namespace as a single-element list. Result
    order is the API list order — never re-sorted.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names unions, over every tenant namespace, the service
    `key` values of `status.services` of every @TenantInstance listed there — including the
    calling instance's own services — sorts the concatenated keys lexicographically and keeps
    duplicates; each namespace is read with a full `api.list`, not metadata-only.
  Every Rhai-facing bridge in this file drives its async body through @tokio::task::block_in_place
    combined with @tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on, so it must run on a multi-thread runtime
    (@tokio::task::block_in_place panics on a current-thread runtime), and failures reach scripts
    as @crate::rhai_err strings. @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name propagates every
    underlying failure that way, while @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_namespaces and
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_services_names only propagate their @serde_json round-trip
    conversion errors.
  @tenant_rhai_register registers the type under the script name `TenantInstance` and is the
    only bridge exposing the three in-file tenant getters to scripts; the registered
    `options_digest` binds directly to @TenantInstance::get_options_digest (plain @String
    return, no Rhai wrapper), and the registered `get_services` binds to
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_services (joined @String), not to the list-returning
    @TenantInstance::get_services.

Depends on:
  @impl_condition_common! and @impl_condition_children! in ./instance_macros.rs — stamp
    @ApplicationCondition::new with @chrono::Utc::now and supply the generation-carrying
    constructors this type's flow composes, including @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko, @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko, the five ok/ko children-stage pairs, and the
    @ApplicationCondition::init_ko, @ApplicationCondition::init_version_ko and
    @ApplicationCondition::schedule_ko recorders of the `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup` stages.
  @impl_instance_common!(TenantInstance, "TenantInstance") in ./instance_macros.rs — attach the
    status merge-patch (@TenantInstance::patch_status, embedding the call-site kind literal), the
    event recorder (@TenantInstance::send_event), the private rebuild and gating probes
    (@TenantInstance::have_condition, @TenantInstance::get_conditions_excluding) that this file's
    Scenario tests exercise, and the shared lookup, options-digest, tfstate/rhaistate,
    agent/missing and Rhai surface that @tenant_rhai_register republishes.
  @impl_instance_befores!(TenantInstance) in ./instance_macros.rs — attach the children-stage
    setters and the children variant of @TenantInstance::set_status_ready (whose exclusion list
    evicts `InitFrom` and `ScheduleBackup` records on every success close), @TenantInstance::get_services,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_init_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_schedule_backup_failed and
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_init_version with their Rhai bridges.
  @crate::context::get_client_async in ./context.rs — every cluster-read call builds its
    @kube::Client from context at call time; nothing stores a client in the resource.
  @k8s_openapi::api::core::v1::Namespace with @kube::api::Api and @kube::api::ListParams — the
    cluster-wide namespace metadata reads and the tenant label-selector list.
  @crate::Children and @crate::Published in ./lib.rs — the child records stored in the five
    stage lists and the published-service records in `services`, whose `key` fields
    @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names collects through the macro-attached
    @TenantInstance::get_services.
  @crate::Error, @crate::Result, @crate::RhaiRes and @crate::rhai_err in ./lib.rs — the error
    contract propagated by the async getters and flattened to strings at the Rhai bridges.
  @kube::CustomResource, @kube::Resource, @kube::ResourceExt — the derive that generates
    @TenantInstance and the metadata/namespace plumbing behind macro-owned patching.
  @rhai::Engine and @rhai::Dynamic — the engine this file registers the bridge onto and the
    array value the collection wrappers return.
  @tokio::task::block_in_place and @tokio::runtime::Handle — the sync-to-async bridge under the
    three Rhai wrappers.
  @chrono::DateTime<@chrono::Utc> — the condition timestamp type.

Exposes:
  @InitFrom — restore-source struct with public fields @InitFrom::secret_name,
    @InitFrom::sub_path and @InitFrom::version (`@Option<@String>`, wire `secretName`,
    `subPath`, `version`) and @InitFrom::snapshot (required @String); derives @Serialize,
    @Deserialize, @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema. Its doc comments name defaults
    (`backup-settings` secret, `<namespace-name>/<app-slug>` sub-path) this file never applies.
  @TenantInstanceSpec — CRD spec struct with public fields @TenantInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @TenantInstanceSpec::category, @TenantInstanceSpec::package, @TenantInstanceSpec::init_from
    (`@Option<@InitFrom>`, wire `initFrom`) and @TenantInstanceSpec::options
    (`@Option<@serde_json::Map<@String, @serde_json::Value>>`); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize,
    @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema; unknown top-level spec keys are silently dropped (no
    `deny_unknown_fields`).
  @TenantInstance — resource root generated by the @kube::CustomResource derive over
    @TenantInstanceSpec, with fields `spec` (@TenantInstanceSpec) and `status`
    (`@Option<@TenantInstanceStatus>`); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug and
    @JsonSchema via the derive.
  @ConditionsType — install-stage enum in declaration order: `Ready` (@Default), `Installed`,
    `Backuped`, `Restored`, `AgentStarted`, `TofuInstalled`, `BeforeApplied`, `VitalApplied`,
    `ScalableApplied`, `InitFrom`, `ScheduleBackup`, `OtherApplied`, `RhaiApplied`,
    `PostApplied`; serialized as bare variant strings (no `CrdApplied` — the tenant family
    variant is absent by design); derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone,
    @Debug, @JsonSchema, @Default.
  @ConditionsStatus — enum `True` or `False`, serialized as those strings, with @Default
    selecting `True`; derives @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema, @Default.
  @ApplicationCondition — one recorded condition, module-local to ./instancetenant.rs and
    distinct from the same-named types of the sibling instance modules, with public fields
    @ApplicationCondition::last_transition_time (`@Option<@chrono::DateTime<@chrono::Utc>>`),
    @ApplicationCondition::message, @ApplicationCondition::condition_type,
    @ApplicationCondition::status and @ApplicationCondition::generation (`@i64`); derives @Eq
    and @PartialEq, compared field-by-field by the macro-owned dedup gate.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_common!: @ApplicationCondition::new,
    @ApplicationCondition::ready_ok, @ApplicationCondition::ready_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::installed_ok, @ApplicationCondition::installed_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::agent_started, @ApplicationCondition::missing_package,
    @ApplicationCondition::missing_box, @ApplicationCondition::missing_requirement,
    @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ok, @ApplicationCondition::tofu_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ok, @ApplicationCondition::rhai_ko.
  Constructors attached by @impl_condition_children!: @ApplicationCondition::before_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::before_ko, @ApplicationCondition::vital_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::vital_ko, @ApplicationCondition::scalable_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::scalable_ko, @ApplicationCondition::other_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::other_ko, @ApplicationCondition::post_ok,
    @ApplicationCondition::post_ko, @ApplicationCondition::init_ko,
    @ApplicationCondition::init_version_ko and @ApplicationCondition::schedule_ko.
  @TenantInstanceStatus — status struct with public fields @TenantInstanceStatus::conditions
    (`@Vec<@ApplicationCondition>`, required), @TenantInstanceStatus::tag,
    @TenantInstanceStatus::digest, @TenantInstanceStatus::tfstate,
    @TenantInstanceStatus::rhaistate (`@Option<@String>`), @TenantInstanceStatus::befores,
    @TenantInstanceStatus::vitals, @TenantInstanceStatus::scalables,
    @TenantInstanceStatus::others, @TenantInstanceStatus::posts (`@Option<@Vec<@crate::Children>>`),
    and @TenantInstanceStatus::services (`@Option<@Vec<@crate::Published>>`); derives
    @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug, @JsonSchema.
  @TenantInstance::have_child — child-state probe.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name, @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces and
    @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names — the async tenant-identity getters.
  @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name, @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_namespaces and
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_services_names — the synchronous Rhai bridges over those
    getters.
  Methods attached by @impl_instance_common!: async @TenantInstance::get, @TenantInstance::list,
    @TenantInstance::get_options_digest, @TenantInstance::get_tfstate,
    @TenantInstance::get_rhaistate, @TenantInstance::set_tfstate,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_tofu_failed, @TenantInstance::set_rhaistate,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_rhai_failed, @TenantInstance::set_agent_started,
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_box, @TenantInstance::set_missing_package and
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_requirement; Rhai bridges @TenantInstance::rhai_get,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_list, @TenantInstance::get_metadata, @TenantInstance::get_spec,
    @TenantInstance::get_status, @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tfstate,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_rhaistate, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_ready,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_tfstate, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_tofu_failed,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_rhaistate, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_rhai_failed,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_agent_started, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_box,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_package and @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_requirement.
  Methods attached by @impl_instance_befores!: async @TenantInstance::set_status_ready,
    @TenantInstance::get_services, @TenantInstance::get_services_string,
    @TenantInstance::set_services, @TenantInstance::set_status_befores,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_before_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_vitals,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_vital_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_scalables,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_scalable_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_others,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_other_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_posts,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_post_failed, @TenantInstance::set_status_init_failed,
    @TenantInstance::set_status_schedule_backup_failed and
    @TenantInstance::set_missing_init_version; Rhai bridges @TenantInstance::rhai_set_services,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_services, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_befores,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_before_failed, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_vitals,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_vital_failed, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_scalables,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_scalable_failed, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_others,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_other_failed, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_posts,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_post_failed, @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_init_failed,
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_schedule_backup_failed and
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_init_version.
  @tenant_rhai_register — installs the script-visible surface on a caller @rhai::Engine under
    the registered type name `TenantInstance`: free functions `get_tenant_instance` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get, `get_tenant_name` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name,
    `get_tenant_namespaces` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_namespaces,
    `get_tenant_services_names` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_services_names,
    `list_tenant_instance` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_list, `options_digest` ->
    @TenantInstance::get_options_digest, `get_tfstate` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tfstate,
    `get_rhaistate` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_rhaistate, `set_agent_started` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_agent_started, `set_missing_box` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_box, `set_missing_package` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_package, `set_missing_requirement` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_requirement, `set_missing_init_version` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_missing_init_version, `set_status_ready` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_ready, `set_status_befores` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_befores, `set_status_before_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_before_failed, `set_status_vitals` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_vitals, `set_status_vital_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_vital_failed, `set_status_scalables` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_scalables, `set_status_scalable_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_scalable_failed, `set_status_others` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_others, `set_status_other_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_other_failed, `set_status_posts` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_posts, `set_status_post_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_post_failed, `set_tfstate` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_tfstate, `set_status_tofu_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_tofu_failed, `set_rhaistate` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_rhaistate, `set_services` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_set_services,
    `get_services` -> @TenantInstance::rhai_get_services, `set_status_rhai_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_rhai_failed, `set_status_schedule_backup_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_schedule_backup_failed, `set_status_init_failed` ->
    @TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_init_failed; property getters `metadata` ->
    @TenantInstance::get_metadata, `spec` -> @TenantInstance::get_spec, `status` ->
    @TenantInstance::get_status.

Accepts:
  Install coordinates as free-form strings in @TenantInstanceSpec::jukebox,
    @TenantInstanceSpec::category and @TenantInstanceSpec::package, plus
    @TenantInstanceSpec::options as any JSON object map or @None, and @TenantInstanceSpec::init_from
    as an `@InitFrom` object or @None — this file only digests `options` (macro) and never
    interprets `initFrom`.
  The three async getters take only `&self` and read the cluster: instance namespace from
    `metadata`, process environment `TENANT_LABEL` read per call.
  The three in-file Rhai bridges take `&mut self` (Rhai registration shape) and no arguments.
  @tenant_rhai_register takes a borrowed @rhai::Engine to decorate.
  Macro-attached setters accept the argument shapes and @rhai::Dynamic conversions frozen in
    ./instance_macros.sdd.

Returns:
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name returns @crate::Result<@String> — the tenant label value or
    the fallback namespace name.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces returns @crate::Result<@Vec<@String>> in API order,
    the single own namespace when unlabeled.
  @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names returns @crate::Result<@Vec<@String>> sorted
    lexicographically, duplicates kept, own services included.
  @TenantInstance::have_child returns a `@bool` per the probe rules above.
  @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name returns @crate::RhaiRes<@String>; the two collection
    bridges return @crate::RhaiRes<@rhai::Dynamic> — a @rhai string array on success, or the
    plain @rhai string `""` when the underlying getter failed.
  Macro-attached mutators return @crate::Result<@TenantInstance> carrying the server-merged
    object; @tenant_rhai_register returns nothing.

Raises:
  @crate::Error::Other(`TenantInstance has no namespace`) from @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name
    and @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces when `metadata.namespace` is @None.
  @crate::Error::KubeError when the namespace metadata `get_metadata`, the selector
    `list_metadata`, or the per-namespace instance `list` fails;
    @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names also propagates both earlier error variants
    through its inner @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces call (its doc comment names only
    `KubeError`).
  @crate::Error::SerializationError inside @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_namespaces and
    @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_services_names when the @serde_json round-trip to
    @rhai::Dynamic fails.
  Every in-file Rhai bridge instead surfaces @rhai::EvalAltResult produced by @crate::rhai_err —
    the typed @crate::Error is flattened into its message string; @tokio::task::block_in_place
    panics on a current-thread runtime.

Handles:
  Missing `metadata.namespace` — typed @crate::Error::Other before any cluster call.
  Namespace with no labels, or labels without the tenant key — tenant name falls back to the
    namespace name and the namespace list to the single own namespace.
  `TENANT_LABEL` set in the process environment — the non-default label key is used on both
    metadata paths.
  Namespace metadata answers without a name during the selector list — that entry is dropped by
    `filter_map`.
  Async getter failure reached through the two collection Rhai bridges — scripts receive the
    plain string `""` instead of an array or an error.
  @TenantInstanceStatus absent — @TenantInstance::have_child answers `false`; macro-owned
    rebuilds and service reads start from empty sets.

