      so a cluster read failure is indistinguishable from an empty tenant; their
      @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_name sibling propagates every failure as a Rhai error
      instead. Decide later whether the swallow is kept and the three wrappers unified.
  [?] @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names includes the calling instance's own service
      keys and keeps duplicates across tenant namespaces (sort without dedup), and its doc
      comment promises `Error::KubeError` only while `Error::Other` propagates through the inner
      namespaces call. Confirm the self-inclusion/duplication and fix the doc.
  [?] @InitFrom doc comments promise defaults (`backup-settings` secret,
      `<namespace-name>/<app-slug>` sub-path) that nothing in this file applies — the fields
      travel as @None until some consumer interprets them. Decide where the defaults must be
      documented and applied (candidate consumer owns them).
  [?] @test_spec_version_top_level_ignored freezes that a misplaced top-level spec `version`
      key is silently dropped (no `deny_unknown_fields`), which reads like a migration guard
      from a schema where the version sat at spec top level. Decide later whether unknown keys
      should be rejected to surface the misplacement.
  [?] @TenantInstance::have_child is asymmetric like its siblings: `tfstate`/`rhaistate` as
      @Some of the empty string count as a child while @Some of an empty list in the five child
      keys does not. Confirm the asymmetry is intended (same finding in ./instancesystem.sdd).
  [?] Dérives @std::default::Default on @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus have no
      detectable use repo-wide (same finding in ./instancesystem.sdd). Decide later whether
      they stay.
  [?] The @TenantInstanceSpec struct doc `Describe a source of vynil packages jukebox` is
      inherited from the `JukeBox` model and does not describe this CRD (the CRD doc string
      itself is correct) — confirm the intended wording (same drift in ./instancesystem.sdd).
  [?] @ApplicationCondition, @ConditionsType and @ConditionsStatus are redeclared per instance
      module with byte-identical shapes; the macros resolve them against the call site (see
      ./instance_macros.sdd). Decide later whether one shared type replaces the three copies.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test, the Tasks decisions are closed, and
    `cargo test -p common`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`,
    `cargo +nightly fmt --check` and `specdd lint` are green.

Scenario: initFrom keeps the requested restore version
  Given YAML `snapshot: "abc123"` with `version: "1.5.0"`
  When it deserializes into @InitFrom
  Then @InitFrom::version is @Some(`1.5.0`)
  Maps to test @test_init_from_with_version

Scenario: initFrom without a version deserializes to None
  Given YAML carrying only `snapshot: "abc123"`
  When it deserializes into @InitFrom
  Then @InitFrom::version is @None — the version is optional while `snapshot` is required
  Maps to test @test_init_from_without_version

Scenario: Misplaced top-level spec version is ignored
  Given spec YAML with `jukebox`, `category`, `package` and a misplaced top-level
    `version: "1.0.0"` instead of an `initFrom` block
  When it deserializes into @TenantInstanceSpec
  Then parsing succeeds, @TenantInstanceSpec::jukebox is `my-juke` and
    @TenantInstanceSpec::init_from is @None — unknown top-level keys are dropped silently
  Maps to test @test_spec_version_top_level_ignored

Scenario: Init-version failure message carries the error identifier
  Given this module expanded @impl_condition_common! and @impl_condition_children!
  When @ApplicationCondition::init_version_ko is called with version `1.5.0` and generation `3`
  Then the record is `False`/`InitFrom` and its message contains both `E_INIT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND`
    and `1.5.0`, at generation `3`
  Maps to test @test_init_version_ko_message_contains_error_id_and_version

Scenario: Gate probe detects an already-stored init-version failure
  Given a client-side-built @TenantInstance whose stored conditions hold the exact
    @ApplicationCondition::init_version_ko record
  When the private @have_condition probe runs against that record
  Then it answers `true`, confirming the four-field (type, generation, status, message)
    equality gate the macro setters consult before patching
  Maps to test @test_have_condition_detects_init_version_ko

Scenario: Tenant name falls back to the namespace when unlabeled
  Given a @TenantInstance in namespace `team-a` whose @Namespace metadata carries no
    `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant` label (or `TENANT_LABEL` names a key it lacks)
  When @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name is awaited
  Then it returns `team-a` and @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces returns the single
    element `team-a`
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet; see the open task above.

Scenario: Labeled tenant gathers namespaces and service names across them
  Given namespace `team-a` labeled `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant`=`acme` and another namespace
    `team-a-extra` with the same label, each holding @TenantInstance objects publishing service
    keys, including the calling instance itself
  When @TenantInstance::get_tenant_name is awaited it returns `acme`
  And @TenantInstance::get_tenant_namespaces lists both namespaces by the selector
    `vynil.solidite.fr/tenant==acme`
  And @TenantInstance::get_tenant_services_names returns every key sorted with duplicates kept
    and the instance's own keys included
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Collection bridges swallow cluster failures into an empty string
  Given a @rhai script whose cluster is unreachable so the registered `get_tenant_namespaces`
    underlying getter fails
  When @TenantInstance::rhai_get_tenant_namespaces runs
  Then the script receives the plain @rhai string `""`, not an array and not an error, while
    the same failure through the registered `get_tenant_name` surfaces as a @rhai::EvalAltResult
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.

Scenario: Child-state probe
  Given a @TenantInstance with no status at all, @TenantInstance::have_child answers `false`
  But when only `rhaistate` or only `tfstate` is `@Some`, even the empty string, it answers
    `true`
  And when the five child lists are all `@Some` of empty lists and no state is stored, it
    answers `false`
  And when any one of them is `@Some` of one entry, it answers `true`
  No mapped test exists for this Scenario yet.
